  "title": "Beneš Conjecture (graph-theoretic form)",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Problem ( $\\dag$ ) Find a sufficient condition for a straight $\\ell$-stage graph to be rearrangeable. In particular, what about a straight uniform graph?\n\nConjecture ( $\\diamond$ ) Let $L$ be a simple regular ordered $2$-stage graph. Suppose that the graph $L^m$ is externally connected, for some $m\\ge1$. Then the graph $L^{2m}$ is rearrangeable.",
